{{!-- The design's numbered pagination. Registered as `pagination`, so it REPLACES the one Ghost
ships: `{{pagination}}` resolves the partial by that name and the theme's copy wins.

	{{pagination pt="pt-14"}}    the homepage's, directly below the article grid
	{{pagination pt="pt-12"}}    the Feed's, directly below the list or grid

	pt    the section's top padding — the two Surfaces sit the control at different heights

The wrapper is inside this partial rather than at the call site so a publication with one page
of posts gets no empty band: there is nothing to move to, so neither the control nor its
padding renders. The design source always draws it because its demo has exactly one page.

WHICH NUMBERS APPEAR, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE DESIGN'S FIVE. Ghost's pagination context carries
`page`, `pages`, `prev`, `next`, `total` and `limit`, and Handlebars has no arithmetic — Ghost
ships no `math` helper, so the only page numbers this template can name are the ones already in
that context: 1 (a literal), `prev`, `page`, `next` and `pages`. Over six pages that renders
`1 2 … 6` · `1 2 3 … 6` · `1 2 3 4 … 6` · `1 … 3 4 5 … 6` · `1 … 4 5 6` · `1 … 5 6`, where the
design draws `1 2 3 … 6` on its one page. The gap on the left is exact (`prev > 2` is a literal
comparison, so it can never appear between 1 and 2); the gap on the right can only be tested as
`pages > next`, so on page 4 of six the ellipsis stands in for a single hidden page.
Recorded, with its measured cost, in DECISIONS.md.

`prev` and `next` are `null` at the ends of the range. The step keeps its box either way — the
design draws both arrows on page 1, muted on the left and inked on the right, which is exactly
a disabled previous and a live next — so the inert one renders as a `span` rather than as a
link to nowhere. --}}
{{#match pages ">" 1}}
	<section
		aria-label="{{t "Pagination"}}"
		class="container {{#if pt}}{{pt}}{{else}}pt-12{{/if}}">
		<nav
			aria-label="{{t "Pagination"}}"
			class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2">

			{{#if prev}}
				<a
					href="{{page_url prev}}"
					rel="prev"
					aria-label="{{t "Previous page"}}"
					class="border-border font-ui text-muted hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-2.5 text-sm no-underline">
					<span
						aria-hidden="true"
						class="font-[system-ui,sans-serif]">←</span>
				</a>
			{{else}}
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="border-border font-ui text-muted rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-2.5 text-sm">
					<span class="font-[system-ui,sans-serif]">←</span>
				</span>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Page 1 is always in the control, and on page 1 it is the current page. --}}
			{{#match page 1}}
				{{> "pagination-page" n=1 here=true}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "pagination-page" n=1}}
			{{/match}}

			{{#match prev ">" 2}}
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="text-muted px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">…</span>
			{{/match}}

			{{#match prev ">" 1}}
				{{> "pagination-page" n=prev}}
			{{/match}}

			{{!-- The current page, only where 1 and `pages` have not already drawn it. --}}
			{{#match page ">" 1}}
				{{#match page "<" pages}}
					{{> "pagination-page" n=page here=true}}
				{{/match}}
			{{/match}}

			{{!-- `next` is null on the last page, and a null comparison is not false in JavaScript:
			`null < 6` is true, so both blocks below need the existence guard rather than the
			comparison alone. The same trap does not exist on the left, where `null > 2` is false. --}}
			{{#if next}}
				{{#match next "<" pages}}
					{{> "pagination-page" n=next}}
				{{/match}}

				{{#match pages ">" next}}
					<span
						aria-hidden="true"
						class="text-muted px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">…</span>
				{{/match}}
			{{/if}}

			{{#match page pages}}
				{{> "pagination-page" n=pages here=true}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "pagination-page" n=pages}}
			{{/match}}

			{{#if next}}
				<a
					href="{{page_url next}}"
					rel="next"
					aria-label="{{t "Next page"}}"
					class="border-border font-ui text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-2.5 text-sm no-underline">
					<span
						aria-hidden="true"
						class="font-[system-ui,sans-serif]">→</span>
				</a>
			{{else}}
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="border-border font-ui text-muted rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-2.5 text-sm">
					<span class="font-[system-ui,sans-serif]">→</span>
				</span>
			{{/if}}

		</nav>
	</section>
{{/match}}
